:{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.8.dev4\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev3 - Linux Mint 22.3 (Zena) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Mesa Intel(R) Graphics (ADL GT2) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-1235U (12 threads) - 7.48 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIt seems like polyline/multiline drawing and similar were changed recently to have thinner line lengths when antialiased, likely a bugfix because they used to be surprisingly thick. It seems like to get the old thickness, you need double the width.\n\nThe editor for the Curve resource hasn't changed its widths and is now looking kinda bad.\n\n<img width=\"171\" height=\"120\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d7b4a8bf-8334-47a3-b1bd-1af47dbc1804\" />\n\n^ For example here, the curve is just too thin, and the line to the handle is not even rendering.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nLook at the inpsector when editing any Curve resource.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123190/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123190/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}